<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Safar Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1635</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Safar Pasha was a member of the Georgian Jaqeli family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samtskhe">Samtskhe</a> who converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and became the first governor of the Ottoman Childir Eyalet when the principality was made a province in 1628. The governorship, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhaltsikhe">Akhaltsikhe</a>, remained largely hereditary in his family.</p></div>
